---

<GuideLayout
  title="Wrought Iron Fence, St. George UT"
  description="Wrought iron and ornamental fences in St. George, UT: cost per foot, steel vs. aluminum, finishes for desert sun, front-yard rules, and comparing quotes."
  path={path}
  eyebrow="Material guide · Fences · St. George & Washington County"
  h1="Wrought Iron and Ornamental Fences in St. George: Cost, Metals, and Rules"
  answer={`As of ${COST_AS_OF}, a wrought iron or ornamental metal fence in St. George, UT costs about ${iron.range} per linear foot installed, based on national published ranges, against ${chain.range} for chain-link and ${vinyl.range} for vinyl. Most "wrought iron" quoted today is welded steel or aluminum; it gives an open, decorative fence that can meet the city's front-yard openness rule, and its life depends on the finish.`}
  updated={UPDATED}
  updatedLabel={UPDATED_LABEL}
  article={{ headline: 'Wrought Iron and Ornamental Fences in St. George: Cost, Metals, and Rules', datePublished: UPDATED }}
  faq={faq}
  related={[
    { href: '/fence-installation-st-george-ut/', label: 'Fence installation hub', blurb: 'All materials, heights, and permit rules.' },
    { href: '/fence-and-block-wall-cost-st-george-ut/', label: 'Full cost guide', blurb: 'Every range and source.' },
    { href: '/pool-fence-and-gate-st-george-ut/', label: 'Pool fence and gates', blurb: 'Barrier rules before you order.' },
    { href: '/block-wall-installation-st-george-ut/', label: 'Block walls', blurb: 'Iron panels on block columns.' },
    { href: '/fence-repair-st-george-ut/', label: 'Fence repair', blurb: 'Rust, bent pickets, sagging gates.' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    An ornamental metal fence is the decorative option in St. George: it marks a boundary, frames a view of the red rock,
    and stays open where a solid fence would block the breeze and the sightline. It costs more per foot than chain-link
    and does not give privacy. This guide covers what it costs, what "wrought iron" actually means in a quote, what to
    specify for sun and sprinklers, where the city allows it, and how to compare quotes from independent fence companies.
  </p>

  <h2>What an ornamental fence costs in St. George</h2>
  <CostTable
    caption={`Ornamental fence cost against other materials, as of ${COST_AS_OF}`}
    unit="per linear foot, installed"
    rows={[
      { label: 'Ornamental / wrought iron (HomeAdvisor, national)', range: iron.range, note: iron.note },
      { label: 'Chain-link, for comparison', range: chain.range, note: 'Open and cheapest; utilitarian look.' },
      { label: 'Wood privacy, for comparison', range: wood.range, note: 'Solid privacy; needs sealing in this climate.' },
      { label: 'Vinyl (PVC) privacy, for comparison', range: vinyl.range, note: 'Solid privacy, no finish to maintain.' },
    ]}
  />
  <p>
    Inside the ornamental range, the price moves with the metal, the picket and rail sizes, the height, and how much
    decoration there is. Gates are usually priced on their own and can be a large share of a short run, especially a
    double drive gate or an automated one. No St. George fence company publishes ornamental prices, so these are dated
    published ranges, not local quotes; the <a href="/fence-and-block-wall-cost-st-george-ut/">cost guide</a> lists every
    source and date.
  </p>

  <h2>Steel, aluminum, or custom: what you are buying</h2>
  <IconList items={metals} cols={2} />
  <p>
    The word "wrought" is mostly a style name now. What decides how the fence performs is the metal, the size of the
    pickets and rails, and the finish. A quote that names all three is one you can compare; a quote that just says
    "wrought iron fence, 100 feet" is not.
  </p>

  <h2>Sun, sprinklers, and slopes: what to specify</h2>
  <p>
    St. George tied Utah's all-time high of 117 degrees on July 10, 2021, a reading NOAA's State Climate Extremes
    Committee accepted. Metal does not shrink or warp in that heat the way wood does, but the finish takes years of
    ultraviolet light, and a dark fence gets hot to the touch. The places an ornamental fence fails here are predictable:
    the finish where it was cut or scratched, the base of steel posts, and anywhere the irrigation hits every day.
  </p>
  <IconList items={desertSpec} cols={2} />

  <h2>Front yards, height, and permits under city code</h2>
  <p>
    Height and openness are governed by St. George City Code
    <a href="https://stgeorge.municipal.codes/Code/10-18-1" rel="noopener">§10-18-1</a>. In most zones, front-yard fences
    are capped at 4 feet and side and rear-yard fences at 6 feet 4 inches, and within 10 feet behind the sidewalk only
    decorative fences that are at least 50 percent open are allowed. An open picket fence is the classic way to meet that
    rule, so ornamental metal is often the material that lets a front yard be fenced at all. Check the actual spacing of
    the pickets you are buying. Under <a href="https://stgeorge.municipal.codes/Code/10-18-5" rel="noopener">§10-18-5</a>,
    any fence in a front setback needs a permit; the <a href="/fence-permit-st-george-ut/">permit guide</a> covers the
    application. Washington, Hurricane, Ivins and Santa Clara have their own codes; see the
    <a href="/washington-county-fence-service-areas/">service area guide</a>. Before any post holes are dug, the company
    should call Blue Stakes of Utah to locate buried utilities.
  </p>

  <h2>HOAs and pools</h2>
  <p>
    Many St. George HOAs favor ornamental metal for lot lines that face a street, golf course or open space, because it
    keeps views open, and they commonly set the color and style. Get your HOA's written fence standard before you get
    quotes; the <a href="/hoa-fence-requirements-st-george-ut/">HOA fence guide</a> explains how those rules sit on top of
    city code. Around a pool, an ornamental fence has to meet pool-barrier rules on height, picket gaps, climbable rails
    and gate hardware. Read the <a href="/pool-fence-and-gate-st-george-ut/">pool fence and gate guide</a> and confirm
    the current rule with the city before you order a pool run.
  </p>

  <h2>Repairing an ornamental fence</h2>
  <p>
    Bent pickets can often be straightened or replaced individually, a sagging gate re-hung, and surface rust treated and
    refinished before it spreads. HomeGuide's published repair ranges start at {repair.minor} for minor work, with a
    single post around {repair.post} and gate repair at {repair.gate}. When steel posts have rusted through at the ground
    along a whole run, new posts or a new fence is the better spend. The
    <a href="/fence-repair-st-george-ut/">fence repair guide</a> walks through that decision.
  </p>

  <h2>How to compare ornamental fence quotes</h2>
  <IconList items={compareSteps} />
  <p>
    Confirm the company's Utah license status with the
    <a href="https://secure.utah.gov/llv/search/index.html" rel="noopener">DOPL license lookup</a> and ask for proof of
    insurance; the <a href="/licensed-fence-contractor-compare-st-george-ut/">license guide</a> explains what the record
    shows. If you want help finding independent local companies to quote, the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>
    describes how matching works.
  </p>

  <p class="sgfw-note">
    Sources: HomeAdvisor, <a href="https://www.homeadvisor.com/cost/fencing/install-a-wrought-iron-fence/" rel="noopener">"Wrought Iron Fence Cost"</a> (updated June 19, 2026);
    NerdWallet, <a href="https://www.nerdwallet.com/home-ownership/home-improvement/learn/cost-to-install-a-fence" rel="noopener">"Cost to Install a Fence"</a> (updated July 10, 2025);
    HomeGuide, <a href="https://homeguide.com/costs/fence-repair-cost" rel="noopener">"Fence Repair Cost"</a> (updated February 20, 2026);
    NOAA NCEI, <a href="https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/monitoring-content/extremes/scec/reports/20220708-Utah-Maximum-Temperature.pdf" rel="noopener">State Climate Extremes Committee report, Utah maximum temperature</a> (July 2022);
    Blue Stakes of Utah, <a href="https://www.bluestakes.org/" rel="noopener">bluestakes.org</a>;
    St. George City Code <a href="https://stgeorge.municipal.codes/Code/10-18-1" rel="noopener">§10-18-1</a> and
    <a href="https://stgeorge.municipal.codes/Code/10-18-5" rel="noopener">§10-18-5</a> (checked September 26, 2026).
  </p>
